# DECLARED COUNT of occurrences of a pwg-branded ontology namespace.
# See scripts/verify_no_foreign_ontology_namespace.sh for why this exists.
#
# THE BASIS OF THIS NUMBER CHANGED, and saying so is the whole point of this
# comment. A ratchet number that silently changes basis is not evidence about
# anything: comparing it to the previous number compares two different
# questions and reads as a regression that never happened.
#
#   PREVIOUS BASIS   276, counting the unregistered domain only, and
#                    excluding nothing.
#
#   THIS BASIS       294, measured 2026-08-17 on 7cc2a6f, counting BOTH
#                    pwg-branded domains and excluding the gate's own three
#                    files:
#
#                        unregistered domain    278
#                        mDNS-reserved domain    16
#                        --------------------------
#                        total                  294   across 67 files
#
# WHY 294 AND NOT 292. The 292 in the first draft of this change was measured
# before four PRs landed on main, and with an exclusion pathspec that named
# `tests/test_...` when the test actually lives at `scripts/tests/`. A
# pathspec naming a file that does not exist excludes nothing and git says
# nothing, so the gate went on counting one occurrence inside its own test.
# Both errors are corrected here and the number was re-measured rather than
# adjusted.
#
# THE EXCLUSIONS EXIST BECAUSE THE INSTRUMENT MUST NOT MEASURE ITSELF. The
# gate, this file and the gate's test all NAME the domains in prose in order
# to explain what they are for. Without the exclusions, widening the regex
# raised the number purely because the new comment mentioned the new domain.
#
# THIS NUMBER MAY ONLY GO DOWN FROM HERE. Lower it in the same commit that
# removes occurrences. It reaches 0 when the source repos are migrated and
# re-vendored, and then it stays at 0 forever.
294
